// M8h1b town scenario (docs/plans/M8H1B-TOWNS.md §6, decision #3): the market town of the
// `market-town` recipe. A Blue team (M1 platoon and M2 platoon with three squads) holds the
// north edge of the town against a Red motor-rifle attack from the north, through the woods:
// three T-72B platoons (in service from 1985) and two BMP platoons with squads, under the
// commander AI. Tanks without infantry keep out of the town (built-up avoidance); the BMPs
// dismount short of it and the squads go in first.
// Play as Blue: put the squads in the blocks on the edge (OCCUPY BUILDINGS FACING...), keep the
// tanks on the flanks where they see the approach, and do not let them be caught in the streets.
(
    id: "m8h-town",
    name: "THE MARKET TOWN",
    date: (1987, 6, 15),
    start_time_s: 32400, // 09:00
    map: (id: "town", recipe: "market-town", seed: 42, size_m: 8000.0),
    seed: 3,
    briefing: "SITUATION: A RED MOTOR-RIFLE FORCE (T-72B TANKS AND BMP INFANTRY FIGHTING VEHICLES) ADVANCES ON THE TOWN FROM THE NORTH, THROUGH THE WOODS ABOVE IT.\n\nMISSION: 1ST PLATOON (M1) AND 3RD PLATOON (M2 BRADLEY WITH THREE RIFLE SQUADS) HOLD THE TOWN FOR 40 MINUTES. RED WINS BY HOLDING THE TOWN UNCONTESTED FOR 2 MINUTES. A SIDE THAT LOSES 70 % OF ITS VEHICLES LOSES.\n\nNOTES: THE OLD CORE IS CLOSED BLOCKS AROUND COURTYARDS WITH NARROW STREETS; THE NORTH EDGE IS HOUSES WITH GARDENS AND A FEW LARGE SHEDS; THE WOODS REACH ALMOST TO IT. SQUADS IN THE EDGE BLOCKS SEE THE APPROACH; TANKS IN THE STREETS DO NOT. RED TANKS WILL NOT ENTER THE TOWN WITHOUT THEIR INFANTRY.",
    objectives: [(name: "TOWN", centre: (4200.0, 3400.0), radius_m: 650.0)],
    victory: (time_limit_s: 2400.0, objective: "TOWN", attacker: 1, destroyed_fraction: 0.7),
    sides: [
